  "formal_correct_answer": "44",
  "mechanism": "Use four side color groups on short existing outer-edge runs, assigning each real corner to both adjacent sides and inviting duplicate corner counting.",
  "mathematical_solution": {
    "proof": "A one-square-wide border around n-by-n unit picture uses (n+2)^2-n^2=4n+4 tiles. The32 tiles on7cm imply tile side1cm from4(7/s+1)=32. New n=10 needs44.",
    "correct": "44",
    "wrong": "48",
    "wrong_derivation": "Four12-tile sides include the same four corner squares twice:4*12=48. Subtract4 yields44."
  },
